Subject: [PATCH] easymesh translator: lnf_radius VAPs stay out of EasyMesh, like hotspot VAPs

No EasyMesh haul type maps to an lnf_radius VAP (convert_vap_name_to_hault_type): the
controller cannot configure one, yet the translator reported it to the agent, which
listed it in its AP Operational BSS. RDK's controller accepts a Topology Response only
when every operational BSS carries one of its network SSIDs (is_ssid_match): with an
lnf_radius VAP the gateway runs itself, every Topology Response of the co-located agent
failed ("SSID misconfiguration"), its radios stayed in topo_sync_pending, candidate
queries to them were refused with Error_Not_Ready and steers from its BSSes waited
until the clients' association timed out. Applying the controller's settings, the
translator also reset the VAP (disabled, OneWifi's default SSID and security).

The EMOSA pods' bootstrap SSID is such a VAP (emosa-lab spec 8.2: a fronthaul-type
pod-backhaul SSID the gateway provides, on its own bridge, outside the controller's
networks). lnf_radius VAPs are now skipped wherever hotspot VAPs are, in both
directions, and their stations are not reported as the agent's clients: the VAP is
OneWifi's alone, as a hotspot VAP is (rdk-1004, 6 October 2026).

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
+++ b/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
@@ -1323,7 +1323,10 @@
         vap_map = &radio->vaps.vap_map;
         for (unsigned int j = 0; j < radio->vaps.num_vaps; j++) {
             vap = &vap_map->vap_array[j];
-            if (is_vap_hotspot(wifi_prop,vap->vap_index) == true) {
+            /* lnf_radius maps to no EasyMesh haul type: a gateway-local VAP the
+             * controller cannot configure, kept out of EasyMesh like hotspot VAPs */
+            if ((is_vap_hotspot(wifi_prop,vap->vap_index) == true) ||
+                (is_vap_lnf_radius(wifi_prop, vap->vap_index) == TRUE)) {
                 continue;
             }
             bss_count++;
@@ -1582,6 +1585,11 @@
